## 1. What this round does

The adversarial round 1 returned `fail` with three blocking findings and fourteen other findings.
Red pinned failing cases for F1, F2, F3, F4, F6, F8, F9, F10, and F11 in commit `622a0fa5`. The PM
decided F5 and F12 in commit `9fee6e88`. This round fixes the nine pinned findings in the two
scripts, keeps Mom's rows and her five artifact hashes unchanged, and records the map.

## 2. The finding-to-fix map

| Finding | The fix |
| -------- | ------ |
| F1 | `scripts/sprout-cast-panel.mjs` holds `DRAWING_CHINS`, the chin row of each drawing from `docs/chibi-sprouts/redesign-2026-11-23.md` (Dad 435, Grandma 572, Grandpa 495, Tom 583, Lily 574). The head band of a drawing runs from its crown row to its chin row, so the head never reads the body. The drawing mask drops the stray ink of a scanned page, the window is centred on the head axis, and the five committed drawings write their panels. |
| F2 | The Lily side-chin guard reads the colour of the frontmost pixel of the alpha-128 side mask at any alpha, and the guard fires unless that pixel is skin. An antialiased hair edge and a coloured pixel both fail. |
| F3 | The cast sheet applies the head-fit rule and the figure-top rule to every sheet cell, and every sheet cell prints and captions its crop state. The sheet reads the same lit front renders as the panel, so it uses the same head limit. |
| F4 | The face-mark exclusion drops the mark's own region, the pixels of the declared colour and the one-pixel blend edge around them. The eye blobs of the mask without that region stay in the eye mask, so a painted iris that sits close to the mark colour in the palette still reads as an eye. |
| F6 | Both scripts accept only their known options, each with its own value. An unknown argument, a repeated option, or a missing value is refused with one named line before any read or write. |
| F8 | Every record, render, and drawing of every target is read before the first write, and every PNG is written by a temporary file and a rename. |
| F9 | A record must hold the eleven table rows in table order plus `rows.lit`, or the run exits 1 with `record <name>: rows incomplete`. The caption prints `/11`. |
| F10 | The destination walk catches `ENOTDIR` and names the parent that is a regular file. |
| F11 | The destination walk refuses a file with more than one name, so a hard link is refused as `destination is a link`. |

F5 and F12 are the PM decisions of commit `9fee6e88`: the eye-component width limit stays at 0.60
of the head width, and the cell scale stays the clamped nearest-neighbour sampling.

